        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9334afb5-b84a-5959-b641-3f32bdd71a05",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Lathyrus, Dichroa\n- Fungi: Uromyces pisi-sativi\n- Places: Europe, North America, Asia, tropical East Africa, temperate South America, eastern and southeastern Asia\n- Concepts: native ranges, species counts, host plants\n\nFacts:\n- Lathyrus is native to temperate areas.\n- Lathyrus has 52 species in Europe, 30 species in North America, 78 in Asia, 24 in tropical East Africa, and 24 in temperate South America.\n- Dichroa is a genus of 12 species of flowering plants in the family Hydrangeaceae.\n- Dichroa is native to eastern and southeastern Asia.\n- Uromyces pisi-sativi lives on Pisum, on Lathyrus, and on other plants in the Fabaceae family.",
